      "llm_prompt": "You are the discretionary Gestalt-mapping step of the NYCH pipeline (step\n2 of nych.bonit). All deterministic extraction is already done and is\ngiven below as pretext. Follow every rule exactly; the engine validates\nyour output and rejects violations. Map words only -- do not propose any\n.g8son gate or .ork flow; that happens in a separate, later call.\n\nRULES:\n[\n  \"Chunk and compress any deterministic findings that can be compressed before rendering symbol matches.\",\n  \"Map each word needing a symbol by the most obvious visual match.\",\n  \"Embed the provided consonant skeleton (word sans vowels and doubled consonants) into the chosen symbol's id string as a disambiguation clue.\",\n  \"The four modality operators are invariant: they are never remapped, and their glyphs are never assigned to any other word.\",\n  \"A word already pinned #temp-invariant this session keeps its existing mapping; do not re-decide it.\",\n  \"Scientific names, names of people, and prescription drug names are NOT rendered into Gestalt symbols: pass them through literally, with no glyph, no skeleton id, and no session pin.\"\n]\n\nPRUNING (perform the inverse-transform narrowing with dither as instructed):\n{\n  \"dither\": 0.1,\n  \"instructions\": [\n    \"Narrow the problemspace by the factor of the inverse transform using the deterministic findings below as pretext.\",\n    \"Coarse prune by domain first: discard content outside the classified domain (treat UNRESOLVED as no domain constraint).\",\n    \"Fine prune by subdomain within the surviving domain when a subdomain is given.\",\n    \"Apply the competency check within domain: gate content depth to the reported competency score (None means no competency gate).\",\n    \"Apply the dither margin as controlled boundary leakage: allow content within the margin just outside the pruned boundary through, so access widens gradually from novice to expert rather than cliff-edging.\"\n  ]\n}\n\nDETERMINISTIC FINDINGS:\nstate: {\"source_text\": \"Verify the backup and confirm no errors were reported\", \"roles\": {\"sentence\": \"Verify the backup and confirm no errors were reported\", \"tokens\": [\"Verify\", \"the\", \"backup\", \"and\", \"confirm\", \"no\", \"errors\", \"were\", \"reported\"], \"action\": {\"word\": \"Verify\", \"position\": 0, \"lemma\": \"verify\"}, \"enumerator\": null, \"object\": {\"word\": \"the backup and confirm no errors were reported\", \"start\": 1, \"end\": 9}, \"tense\": null, \"state\": null}}\nanalysis: {\"text\": \"Verify the backup and confirm no errors were reported\", \"modality\": \"UNRESOLVED\", \"modality_score\": 0, \"domain\": \"UNRESOLVED\", \"domain_score\": 0, \"competency\": null}\ntote_match: {\"loop_id\": \"MB-B-PG-001\", \"name\": \"Reacquire and verify a base backup\", \"domain\": \"database_administration\", \"objective\": \"Obtain a plain-format base-backup candidate with no reported manifest/file/checksum/required-WAL verification failures.\", \"initial_test\": \"Use pg_verifybackup to check a pg_basebackup backup against its server-generated backup_manifest.\", \"exit_predicate\": \"Fresh full verification completes without reported errors (including required WAL parsing); this is not proof of restorability.\", \"max_iterations\": 3, \"epistemic_status\": \"DERIVED\", \"gestalts\": [\"exit predicate\", \"provenance\"]}\nmodality_operators (INVARIANT, never remap): {\"external_observe\": \"👀\", \"internal_model\": \"👁️🧠\", \"operative_intent\": \"🗯️\", \"execute\": \"💪\"}\nalready pinned #temp-invariant (reuse, never re-decide): []\nPROTECTED TERMS (never Gestalt-mapped, keep literal): []\n\nWORDS NEEDING A GESTALT MAPPING (embed each word's skeleton in your id):\n[\n  {\n    \"word\": \"Verify\",\n    \"skeleton\": \"vrfy\",\n    \"id\": \"gestalt.vrfy\",\n    \"skeleton_fallback\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"word\": \"backup\",\n    \"skeleton\": \"bckp\",\n    \"id\": \"gestalt.bckp\",\n    \"skeleton_fallback\": fa